# Same override as testkit's own multi-worker/env: worker_processes 4 needs
# PROBER_ALLOW_MULTIWORKER=1 to lift prober_check_conf's default worker!=1
# bail (which assumes a single-worker conf and would misread healthy worker
# rotation as a crash). Every case in multi-worker.rule below carries
# `pid_may_change` to match.
#
# PROBER_PROBE is left at testkit's default (test_ref_probe), NOT
# cache_turbo_probe: this scenario's claim is cross-worker MASTER coherence
# (pid_may_change) plus a cache_turbo HIT on whichever worker answers, and
# neither needs cache_turbo's own zone probe fields. The generic probe is
# also the simpler choice here on its own merits -- see
# CTPROBE-STATIC-ZONE-NO-RELOAD (memory/labs/nginx-cache-turbo-module/
# issues.md) for why cache_turbo_probe is a hard requirement, not a style
# choice, on any scenario that reparses its conf more than once (reload-*);
# this scenario has no reload, so that specific hazard is not why the
# generic probe was picked, but there is still no reason to take on that
# directive's extra registration state for a claim it does not need.
PROBER_ALLOW_MULTIWORKER=1
